  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Determine all triplets of real numbers \\((x, y, z)\\) satisfying the system of equations\n\n\\[\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} y+y^{2} z & =1040 \\\\\nx^{2} z+z^{2} y & =260 \\\\\n(x-y)(y-z)(z-x) & =-540\n\\end{aligned}\\]",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "(16,4,1),(1,16,4)",
    "value": "(16,4,1),(1,16,4)"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2020-p16.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Call the three equations (1), (2), (3). (1)/(2) gives \\(y=4 z .(3)+(1)-(2)\\) gives\n\n\\[\\left(y^{2}-z^{2}\\right) x=15 z^{2} x=240\\]\n\nso \\(z^{2} x=16\\). Therefore\n\n\\[\\begin{aligned}\n& z(x+2 z)^{2}=x^{2} z+z^{2} y+4 z^{2} x=\\frac{81}{5} \\\\\n& z(x-2 z)^{2}=x^{2} z+z^{2} y-4 z^{2} x=\\frac{49}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\\]\n\nso \\(\\left|\\frac{x+2 z}{x-2 z}\\right|=\\frac{9}{7}\\). Thus either \\(x=16 z\\) or \\(x=\\frac{z}{4}\\).\nIf \\(x=16 z\\), then (1) becomes \\(1024 z^{3}+16 z^{3}=1040\\), so \\((x, y, z)=(16,4,1)\\).\nIf \\(x=\\frac{z}{4}\\), then (1) becomes \\(\\frac{1}{4} z^{3}+16 z^{3}=1040\\), so \\((x, y, z)=(1,16,4)\\).",
      "hints": [],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
